-------------
VERSION 1.0.0
-------------
* Follow-up: consolidated Yule's Y/Q/V into one validated helper; added
  validated Cramer, contingency and Sakoda helpers alongside Chuprov's T.
* Fixed ordinal inner-range column metadata for fractional coverage.
* Shared rank-effect, rank-summary, confidence-interval, percentage parsing
  and normality-test routines reduce duplication; moved helpers to R/utils.R.
* Expanded the test suite to 34 blocks; follow-up runtime validation pending.
* Corrected geometric mean and geometric standard deviation, Yule's V,
  Wilson's e and Chuprov's T.
* Ordinal summaries now use stored numeric values; corrected inner ranges
  and handling of ordered variables.
* Corrected paired Hodges-Lehmann estimates and confidence intervals,
  Wilcoxon rank-biserial correlation, Mann-Whitney average ranks and
  tie-corrected z statistics, and one-sided normal-approximation p-values.
* Improved confidence-interval handling, selected-pair extraction and
  Wilcoxon rank descriptives, with three rows per pair.
* Normality tests now run only when selected, handle failures individually,
  and correctly populate grouped results. Added an inference caveat for
  Kolmogorov-Smirnov tests with estimated normal parameters.
* Corrected grouped ECDF and Q-Q plots and within-group standardisation.
  Q-Q plotting uses internal functions without importing qqplotr or qqconf.
* Improved discrete and continuous distribution validation and plotting,
  including hypergeometric labels, probability endpoints and degenerate cases.
* Improved handling of missing, empty, constant and invalid inputs;
  corrected result visibility, invalidation, labels and dependent controls.
* Added diagnostics to the existing Linear Regression controls:
  - Normality: RESET, Shapiro-Wilk, Lilliefors and Anderson-Darling tests;
    classical Breusch-Pagan, Koenker, Goldfeld-Quandt and Harrison-McCabe
    heteroskedasticity tests.
  - Autocorrelation: automatic-lag residual ACF plots and multi-lag
    Durbin-Watson tests using 5,000 residual resamples and seed 123456.
  - Residual plots: residuals versus fitted, scale-location, normal Q-Q
    with histogram inset, and influence plots, plus an influence-index table.
  Added saRa attribution and relevant package references to these outputs.
* Updated dependency declarations and package/method references; reduced
  duplicated code, deprecated plotting calls and raw data stored in plot state.


-------------
VERSION 0.1.2
-------------
*Description and 000.yaml modified.
*Univariate Ordinal and Numerical; and Bivariate Mixed Data: label for quartiles' average is now midhinge.
*Bivariate Mixed Data: Data stacked aes() dependence error now solved.
*Continuous variables: stat_function() dependence error now solved.
*Error in z's Wilcoxon's test computation now solved.


